  "summary": "The paper introduces a quantum Chebyshev transform and orthonormal Chebyshev feature map for gate-based quantum machine learning, demonstrated on simulated 5-qubit lognormal distribution learning with a 14-layer variational ansatz and 1,000,000-shot sampling. It also shows a 2-qubit linear-distribution example where the Chebyshev model tracks P(x)=x better than a Fourier feature-map baseline, but no classical advantage is claimed or demonstrated.",
